<%# `contents` twice over: this wrapper and both chips inside it, so the chips'
    groups end up as items of the composer row's flex container instead of
    stacking. display:contents nests, the gap of the outer row applies to the
    groups either way.

    NO conditional around the chips -- each decides for itself whether it
    applies, and this element renders even when both stay away (see the class
    comment: it is the anchor). %>
<div id="<%= dom_id %>" class="contents">
  <%= render reference_chip %>
  <%= render scope_chip %>
</div>
